                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I feel like this game gets more hate than it deserves.\n\nWhile it doesn't fix the issues from previous titles, it at least improved in other areas, especially in gameplay (can't really call it gameplay still, but it at least feels much smoother and more engaging now), story, and graphics. The pacing is also quite good; I was able to play through the whole game in one sitting without getting bored, which is not something I could say about Season 2.\n\nIt's not even worth mentioning that the choices don't matter,everyone knows already,but I personally feel like this game gives you just a bit more freedom in deciding the main characters' fate (with exceptions, of course), which is probably only the case because the characters in this game don't appear in the next one, so it doesn't really matter. Some of the characters' dialogues are also pretty cringe, but you can usually avoid it, so it didn't bother me that much. I also don't like what they did with Kenny at all, concerning both his appearance and [spoiler]his death[/spoiler].\n\nOverall an 8/10, it's a perfectly serviceable addition to the TWDG franchise, with some small improvements made over the last game.",
